From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] radv: report only what the winsys can do

A winsys that is not amdgpu may lack what RADV assumed every kernel has:

- has_external_fd (radeon_winsys_info): memory, semaphores and fences
  shared as file descriptors. Without it there are no *_fd, dma-buf or
  DRM format modifier extensions and no external fd handle types.
- has_gpu_written_ibs (radeon_info): the CP runs a command buffer the GPU
  wrote; device-generated commands need it.
- has_replayable_va (radeon_info): a buffer can be placed at an address an
  earlier allocation was given; every capture and replay feature needs
  it.

Queue families offer sparse binding only where there is sparse memory,
and host pointer imports and placed maps are aligned to the GPU's pages
where those are larger than the CPU's. amdgpu sets all of these as
before.

